      "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ in terms of the components of $y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\ngives the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})^{2}+(3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})(-{y}_{2})-(-{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & =18{y}_{1}^{2}+24{y}_{2}{y}_{1}+8{y}_{2}^{2}-3{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =18{y}_{1}^{2}+21{y}_{2}{y}_{1}+5{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
